       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to **9,000 mg/day**. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many hospitals cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose of 9 g/day risks serious liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the intended order with your resident or attending, as you would for any order you're unsure about."
